= Requested knowledge =

This page records important knowledge BITwiki should cover or strengthen without creating empty Main-namespace shells first.

'''Requested ≠ canonical.''' A request identifies a coverage need. It becomes durable knowledge only after research, sourcing, modeling, writing, and review.

== Why use a request queue? ==

An empty or generic article hides the difference between ''we have this knowledge'' and ''we intend to research this knowledge.'' A request queue keeps that distinction explicit.

Use this page when:

* a topic is clearly important but no coherent sourced page exists yet;
* a current page is too weak to count as meaningful coverage;
* a portal/category reveals a missing prerequisite or bridge topic;
* a Core/Vital coverage review finds an important gap;
* a domain expansion needs evidence before new schema is introduced.

== Request record ==

For each request, record only what is known:

{| class="wikitable"
! Field !! Meaning
|-
| Proposed title || Likely canonical title; may change after research
|-
| Why it matters || Coverage/navigation/research reason
|-
| Candidate Domain(s) || Existing likely fields; do not invent a Domain to satisfy the request
|-
| Source leads || Strong starting sources, when known
|-
| Needed depth || Simple / Core / Technical / Frontier / full page
|-
| Status || requested / researching / drafting / review / satisfied / declined
|-
| Notes || Ambiguity, overlap, duplicate risk, sensitive-topic considerations
|}

